WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.800
- All right, let's wrap this
hour up with one last story

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:03.880
to delight the senses.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.027
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.027 --> 00:00:08.160
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.260
Chicago has a new top dog
and the trophy to prove it.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:15.180
She earned the title by beating
out more than 4,300 people

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:19.690
by visiting 367 Vienna Beef hot dog stands

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.100
in the Chicago land area,

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.960
and driving about 8,000
miles in just five weeks.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.470
I love this woman.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:28.060
She's so competitive.
(audience laughing)

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.940
That should earn anyone a
trophy, is all I'm saying.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.490
But she didn't just land
herself a cool memento,

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.250
she also won a few other prizes

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.590
she's sharing with the
kids in her community.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.380
Let's get this top dog on the line.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.800
She watches on NBC Chicago at two.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.612
What's up, Stephanie?
(audience cheering)

00:00:44.612 --> 00:00:45.650
- Hi.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.132
How are you?
- Hi.

00:00:47.132 --> 00:00:49.990
So, tell us more about this contest

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:51.840
and how you pulled off the win.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.080
- Yeah, so my boyfriend sent me a tweet

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.750
that Vienna Beef was having
this hot dog stand challenge.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.460
And I am super competitive in anything

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.642
with the word challenge, I am
going to dive right into it.

00:01:01.642 --> 00:01:02.475
(audience laughing)

00:01:02.475 --> 00:01:03.560
So I had one of my friends help me

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.890
and made a Google map,

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:08.276
so I could navigate all around Chicago,

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:11.400
Illinois, Wisconsin as fast as possible.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.380
I'm hyper organized.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.470
I had spreadsheets with me.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.600
I averaged at least 10 stands a day.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.190
I would leave work and then drive an hour

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:20.460
through rush hour traffic
to get to hot dog stands.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.390
One weekend, I drove from Chicago

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:24.650
all the way down to Carbondale and back.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:27.460
So 1200 miles in one weekend.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.240
I would go into hot dog stands,

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.140
and the owners would be super excited

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.100
because the person who was in
second place was just there.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.090
When I was in second place,

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:37.320
the person who was in first
place was there just before me.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.153
So it was super fun.

00:01:38.153 --> 00:01:40.240
It was exciting to get
out and see the state

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.410
and do something new.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:43.610
- And meet all those people.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:45.900
That's so cool. What a cool trip.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.940
So what did you win besides the trophy

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.920
and bragging rights, of course?

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.019
- So other than this amazing trophy,

00:01:52.019 --> 00:01:52.852
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:52.852 --> 00:01:54.213
top dog and bragging rights,
(audience cheering)

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:56.170
I got some cool swag.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.900
I also got sports tickets for four

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.240
for the entire year to all
the different sports arenas

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.160
here in Chicago.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:02.993
- Wow!
- Food and drink

00:02:02.993 --> 00:02:04.840
is included with that.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:09.340
And I also got a $1,000
gift card to Vienna Beef.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:10.750
I work with kids and seniors

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.320
here at the Park District in Chicago,

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.270
so all that money is going right back

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.510
into the kids and seniors

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:19.040
so we can throw huge parties
all year long for these kids.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.120
And then also, Vienna
Beef wants to make sure

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.230
that you are in on the fun too.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.563
So you're gonna get some Chicago hot dogs.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.330
- Look, I can smell it from here,

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.050
and I just saw Justin...

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.330
Thank you, Justin.
- You're welcome.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.926
- I love my job, Justin.

00:02:33.926 --> 00:02:35.450
(audience laughing)

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.760
I just feel in honor of you and your win,

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.320
I should celebrate with you.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.173
So here we go.

00:02:42.118 --> 00:02:47.118
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:02:48.461 --> 00:02:50.080
- That's good.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.210
Oh my God! I would've
never loaded it like this.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:53.450
That's really good.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:54.692
Now I shall.

00:02:54.692 --> 00:02:56.070
Thank you so much, Stephanie,

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.342
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:57.342 --> 00:03:01.601
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:02.680
And that's not all.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.500
Our season-long partner Pilot Pen,

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.520
the go-to pen of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.100
thinks that your mission
and what you're doing

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.680
with the winnings is so great.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.360
So in recognition, they'll be using

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:12.610
their FriXion Erasable Pen

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.893
to write you a check for $1,000.

00:03:14.893 --> 00:03:16.554
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:03:16.554 --> 00:03:17.710
- What?

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.574
Oh my God. That's amazing.

00:03:19.574 --> 00:03:20.407
Thank you.

00:03:20.407 --> 00:03:21.240
- That's amazing.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.806
- Oh my God!
- Well, thank you so much,

00:03:22.806 --> 00:03:24.856
and thank you for this delicious hot dog.

